  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BLENDED FINANCE FACILITY WITH WASH/CLIMATE RISK NEXUS AND GENDER LENS FOR MSMEs &amp; WSPs</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a 3-year intervention &#x2013; in technical Assistance (TA) grant to build the capacity of Sidian Bank to originate, appraise, and finance bankable, affirmative, bankable investments from climate and gender (women) perspective. Sidian Bank has a new impact strategy to lend more towards Climate smart investments that focus on household connection, climate risk adaptation, mitigation, and resilience as well as lending to MSMEs with a special focus on women-led, women-owned or providing sanitation services targeting women.The objective of the proposed project is to facilitate Sidian Bank to lend to these target SMEs and private water service providers up to &#x20ac; 7,407,407 within 3 years. 100% of its portfolio will target climate-smart infrastructure projects focusing on climate risk mitigation, adaptation and resilience, and gender lens financing.</narrative>
  </description>
